Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "How Quittance ends: six ways, and which the company came to.".

  // Endings are tried in the order written; the particular before the general. The Burning and the Slaying are done
  // at the moment they happen. The rest are reached at Reckoning midnight (watch 1248), on what the city has paid.
  Chapter reckoning_midnight "Quittance" when watch(clock) >= 1248 "Midnight on the Cinderwall. The clerk from the Hall of the Five comes out with the Receipt on a board and a hook on a pole, and the crowd, which has not been told to be quiet, is.".


  // ── What resolving it is worth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Milestone m_candle_warned "warned Candlewick Court" worth 100 when candlewickWarned(party).
  Milestone m_candle_stopped "turned the torchmen from Candlewick Court" worth 200 when candlewickSaved(party).
  Milestone m_gasket_warned "warned Gasket Yard" worth 100 when gasketWarned(party).
  Milestone m_gasket_stopped "turned Skelter's men from Gasket Yard" worth 200 when gasketSaved(party).
  Milestone m_tables "found what the Tables were hiding" worth 100 when knows(party, d_tables_paradox).
  Milestone m_book "got Skelter's rent-book" worth 150 when knows(party, d_prewitt_appoints).
  Milestone m_return "learned the Return" worth 150 when returnLearned(party).
  Milestone m_prewitt "turned Sedley Prewitt" worth 400 when prewittTurned(party).
  Milestone m_fire "spoke with the Fire" worth 300 when fireHeard(party).
  Milestone m_motion "carried the motion before the Five" worth 300 when motionCarried(city).
  Milestone m_lit "lit four of the wards" worth 300 when wardsLit(city) >= 4.

  Ending end_burning "The Burning" when fireWrathful(party) "The Fire does not shout. It stands up out of its hearth, which is the size of a threshing-floor, and for the first time in ninety-four years it is the size of the thing it is. You do not see the rest of it. You hear the glass of the Sunk City begin, all together, to remember being soft; you feel the warmth come up through the Exchange like a held breath let go. By the time you reach the surface Policy Row is a street of lit windows, and then of windows that are only light. The brigades come out and stand in rows, Phoenix and Lamprey, on either side of a line of whitewash, and look at the plates over the doors, and cannot decide whose it is. Quittance burns for three days. Afterward the survivors are counted, in Gate Plaza, by clerks who have saved their ledgers, and the number is nearer the Tables than anyone had hoped, and more than anyone could bear. The Receipt is never found. It turns out there was nothing, after all, to hang it on.".
  Ending end_slaying "The Slaying" when fireSlain(party) "It goes out slowly, as large fires do: first the red, then the white, then the long grey breath of ash in the Hearth Below. There is a moment when the glass walls of the Sunk City tick, all at once, like a hundred clocks stopping. Then there is nothing in the city that is warm that has not been made so by somebody's hand. That winter no hearth in Quittance will light, not the Wards' nor the Phoenix's, nor the little red coal in Hearn House; they will burn coke and go on being cold; the cold-lamps will glow, and be glad of it, and be nothing else. The Receipt is hung at midnight on the Cinderwall as the Founders directed, and it is blank, and the city looks at it and understands, a good deal late, what had been signed. Nobody in Quittance will ever be burned again. It is considered by the Offices to be an acceptable loss.".
  Ending general_average "General Average" when watch(clock) >= 1248 and fireTermAverage(party) and motionCarried(city) "On the afternoon of Reckoning the Cinder Ward is emptied, street by street, by brigades of both Offices who for the first time in their history are issued the same bucket. Three thousand people sit on the Cinderwall with their bundles and their cats and watch it, in daylight, in good order, with pie. At the stroke of five a man from the Phoenix puts a taper to the well-head. The First Flue breathes in. The Cinder Ward burns, quickly and cleanly, in an hour, and the Fire, which is not in a hurry, takes what it is owed and nothing it is not; and at midnight the Receipt, hung on its hook, is white from edge to edge, and says, in a notary's capitals, QUIT. The Five Offices meet on the Thursday. They are to pay out for three thousand houses, pro rata, in perpetuity, and the Chairman of the Residuary, who has the sandwiches, is heard to say that it is the first time he has ever felt that the Tables came out. Nobody died. It cost everything.".
  Ending hospitality "The Hospitality Renewed" when watch(clock) >= 1248 and fireTerms(party) and (fireTermKeeper(party) or fireTermNight(party)) "At midnight the Receipt goes up on the Cinderwall as it always did, and it is not blank. It is the colour of a good tea, and it says, in a hand nobody in the city has seen for ninety-four years, RECEIVED, WITH THANKS. The Fire has its terms. A hearth is kept in the Hall of the Five from that winter on, in the place where the plaster was, and a Hearthkeeper sits by it who is not a Hearn. Once a year, on the night of Reckoning, the whole of Quittance lights a fire at once, and nobody is allowed to put it out until morning; and the Offices, who do not believe a word of it, discover that the year's claims on that night are never once more than they can pay. The city goes on being what it was. It is only a little warmer. The inner wards keep their gas.".
  Ending quittance_best "Quittance" when watch(clock) >= 1248 and wardsLit(city) >= 4 and motionCarried(city) and prewittTurned(party) "The coals come home. All night they come, from every ward, in tins and pans and saucepans and a hearse, up Policy Row to the Exchange, and nobody counts them; the Five themselves carry the last of them down the cellar stair, in a line, in their good coats. At midnight on the Cinderwall the clerk hooks the Receipt, and it goes up white as the sun, and there is not a person in Quittance who cannot read it. QUITTANCE. IN FULL. Sedley Prewitt resigns the Chief Underwriting in the morning, and spends the rest of his life, to the horror of the Phoenix, in the Bare Wards, keeping a hearth. His daughter inherits the pencils. The Smokeless Ordinance is amended in the spring by a clause that Cornelia Pettifer is understood to have drafted, which allows every household one fire, and one coal, and the Offices are rather surprised to find that premiums have never been lower. In the Bare Wards, they say, the fires are the same as they were. Only now the brigades come to them.".
  Ending quittance_contested "Quittance, Contested" when watch(clock) >= 1248 and wardsLit(city) >= 4 and motionCarried(city) "The coals come home, though not everyone is glad of it. Sedley Prewitt, who did not turn, sits in the Hall with his hands on the table and watches the Five carry them down; he does not stop them; he does not help. At midnight the Receipt goes up on the Cinderwall, and it is white, and says QUIT, and the crowd cheers, and the Chief Underwriter takes his hat and goes home on foot. There is an inquiry in the spring. The list is found, and produced, and nobody is hanged; a rent-collector is posted to a distant parish; the Phoenix issues a statement of profound regret. The Appointed Losses end, because they are no longer needed, and not because anyone is sorry. It is a good ending. It is the kind that leaves a number of people free to say they always thought so.".
  Ending controlled_loss "The Controlled Loss" when burned(cinder_ward) "At midnight the Cinder Ward burns. It burns from the well-head outwards, and then all at once, and the black chimney in the middle of it stands up through the light like the stalk of something. The brigades are drawn up in the Brickfields, on the whitewash, with their pumps primed, protecting the marked; they watch. A man in a long grey coat is standing at the edge of the Ward with his hat in his hand. He does not move. He has not, you think, expected to be able to bear it, and is finding that he can. At midnight, on the Cinderwall, the Receipt goes up on its hook, and it is the colour of a rose. The city's fires, that year, are lower than at any time in the Tables. In the spring Sedley Prewitt receives the Order of the Sovereign Sun for his services to the public safety. You are paid, as agreed, by a clerk who does not look at you. Three thousand people go to live in the Brickfields with relatives, or in the Reach, or the Wards that are left. It is not a thing the Tables can show. It is what the Tables are for.".
  Ending end_lapse "The Lapse" when watch(clock) >= 1248 "Midnight comes to the Cinderwall and the clerk hooks the Receipt, and it hangs there. It is blank. Not pale, not faint: blank, the clean white of a card nobody has written on. The crowd waits. A child asks if it is broken. The Offices' Chairmen look at one another, along the line, and nobody says anything, because they have all come to the conclusion that the thing they feared is only a form that has not been filled in. The Fire is not wrathful. It has been courteous for ninety-four years. In the cellars of the Old Exchange something lets out a long breath, and goes out; it is not a death, but a leave-taking, and the warmth of the city goes with it. In the morning Quittance finds its hearths cold and its marks unmeaning, and the fires, that winter, are rare: the city does not burn, because there is nothing left in it that will light. The cold-lamps hum. The Offices are paid their premiums. By spring half of Quittance has moved to the country.".
}
